// unresolved is either left out here or given with its uncertainty. The
// quotations from J.F.'s English were checked word for word against the TCP
// transcription.
//
// The letters are the alphabet that Trithemius prints in Book VI of the
// Polygraphia (1518, sig. 2q5v) as one lately made up by an alchemist, which
// the plates stage matched to the cipher of the Cipher Manuscripts on one small
// image of folio 13. They are traced from the Wellcome copy and checked sign by
// sign against the Library of Congress copy and the French of 1561
